cepts, tasks, and references in this tutorial have an `@id`, a `<title>`, and a `<shortdesc>`. Stage 25 makes the short description a house rule.\n- The DOCTYPE names a public identifier, and the catalog finds the DTD.\n- `<section>` is one level deep; deeper structure means another topic.\n- Format, then check your work, every time.\n\n## Next lesson {#next-lesson}\n\n**Checkpoint:** `tutorial/01-concept`. If you use Git, commit your work.\n\nContinue with [Stage 02: first map](/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-02-first-map).\n\nFor the core course, use the [learning path](/dita-tutorial/start-here/learning-path) to skip optional modules.\n\n[Compare this stage with its predecessor](https://github.com/dogsbay/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial/compare/tutorial/00-setup...tutorial/01-concept).\n","mdUrl":"https://dogsbay.ai/dita-tutorial/part-1-topics/stage-01-concept.md"} ?? undefined;
